# Homework 4 - Multiple Linear Regression with Scikit-learn 

This assignment uses multiple linear regression to predict monthly `Sales_Revenue` from five business predictors:

- Advertising Spend
- Website Visits
- Discount Rate
- Sales Staff Hours
- Customer Count

## Objectives
- Load and inspect the business dataset
- Generate descriptive statistics and check for missing values
- Analyze correlations among the predictors and Sales Revenue
- Split the data into 80% training and 20% testing sets
- Build a multiple linear regression model using scikit-learn
- Interpret the model intercept and regression coefficients
- Generate predictions for the testing data
- Calculate residuals
- Evaluate model performance using:
  - Mean Squared Error (MSE)
  - Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
  - R²
- Compare training and testing performance
- Create regression diagnostic visualizations
- Generate Sales Revenue predictions for hypothetical business scenarios
- Review and improve Copilot-generated code

## Visualizations
- Correlation heatmap
- Advertising Spend vs. Sales Revenue scatterplot
- Regression coefficient bar chart
- Actual vs. Predicted Sales scatterplot
- Residual plot

## Files
- Python program for the multiple regression analysis
- `correlation_matrix.csv`
- `regression_predictions.csv`
- `regression_metrics.csv`
- `business_predictions.csv`
- `correlation_heatmap.png`
- `advertising_sales_scatterplot.png`
- `regression_coefficients.png`
- `actual_vs_predicted.png`
- `residual_plot.png`
- Copilot code-review documentation
